            <ArticleTitle>Cardiac CT Imaging of Plaque Vulnerability: Hype or Hope?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>37</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s11886-016-0714-0</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Advances in cardiovascular computed tomography (CT) have resulted in an excellent ability to exclude coronary heart disease (CHD). Anatomical information, functional information, and spectral information can already be obtained with current CT technologies. Moreover, novel developments such as targeted nanoparticle contrast agents, photon-counting CT, and phase contrast CT will further enhance the diagnostic value of cardiovascular CT. This review provides an overview of current state of the art and future cardiovascular CT imaging.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
